  "market_context": "EURUSD in a clear downtrend on the 1-hour chart; price approached a previously identified supply zone, prompting analysis on the 5-minute chart for entry confirmation during London session.",
  "key_observation": "A double top reversal pattern formed inside a marked supply zone on the 5-minute chart, showing momentum loss and aligning with the higher-time-frame bearish bias.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a downtrend on the EURUSD 1-hour chart and marked the prior bullish candle cluster as a supply zone for short opportunities.",
    "Step 2: Zoomed into the 5-minute chart upon price approaching the supply zone to seek entry confirmation.",
    "Step 3: Observed a double top reversal pattern forming within the supply zone, indicating momentum loss and reinforcing bearish bias.",
    "Step 4: Waited for price to pull back to the neckline of the double top before entering.",
    "Step 5: Entered a short position on a long wick rejection candlestick at the neckline, with stop-loss above the swing high and 1:2 risk-to-reward target."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Combining higher-time-frame structure (downtrend + supply zone) with lower-time-frame reversal patterns (double top) and precise price action entry (long wick rejection) increases trade probability and improves R:R.",
